1 0 0 1 58 357 Tm (A different way to work with your thoughts) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 323 Tm () Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 300 Tm (Charles F. Haanel's Master Key System is a structured course of study built around the) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 285 Tm (mind, attention, clear purpose and regular practice. It asks you to slow down and work) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 270 Tm (with one lesson at a time. You read, reflect, complete the exercises and return to the) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 255 Tm (ideas often enough for them to become more than words on a page.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 232 Tm (This matters because reading a powerful idea once is not the same as practising it.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 209 Tm (Daily study gives you a chance to notice the thoughts that pull you towards fear or) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 194 Tm (helplessness-and to practise turning your attention towards what you want to understand,) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 179 Tm (build and do. It encourages you to define a purpose, use concentration and visualisation,) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 164 Tm (and take your ideas into your everyday conduct.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 141 Tm (It is not a magic switch, and it does not remove life's practical challenges. It is a) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 126 Tm (disciplined way to strengthen your inner direction while you meet those challenges.) Tj
